given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Reeve-Daly</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Lander</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Parametric and nonparametric linkage analysis: a unified multipoint approach</article-title><source>Am J Hum Genet</source><year>1996</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>1347</fpage><lpage>1363</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8651312</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pratt</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Daly</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kruglyak</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Exact multipoint quantitative-trait linkage analysis in pedigrees by variance components</article-title><source>Am J Hum Genet</source><year>2000</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>1153</fpage><lpage>1157</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10712227</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/302830</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><sec sec-type="display-objects"><title>Figures and Tables</title><fig position="float" id="F1"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Distribution of observed gender-specific overall crossover frequency in 22 autosomes.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="1471-2156-6-S1-S58-1"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Coefficients in the regression model of recombination rate<sup>a</sup></p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td></td><td align="right">Estimate</td><td align="right">SE</td><td align="right">Z</td><td align="right">P</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">Intercept</td><td align="right">38.48</td><td align="right">1.35</td><td align="right">28.34</td><td align="right">0</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Male</td><td align="right">-15.67</td><td align="right">0.59</td><td align="right">-26.58</td><td align="right">0</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Black, non-Hispanic</td><td align="right">1.66</td><td align="right">1.016</td><td align="right">1.64</td><td align="right">0.101</td></tr><tr><td align="left">White, Hispanic</td><td align="right">-0.71</td><td align="right">0.75</td><td align="right">-0.95</td><td align="right">0.342</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Other ethnicity</td><td align="right">-0.14</td><td align="right">0.94</td><td align="right">-0.14</td><td align="right">0.889</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Age</td><td align="right">-0.025</td><td align="right">0.046</td><td align="right">-0.55</td><td align="right">0.582</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Adyr<sup>b</sup></td><td align="right">0.049</td><td align="right">0.022</td><td align="right">2.21</td><td align="right">0.027</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p><sup>a</sup>White, non-Hispanic is the reference group for ethnicity.</p><p><sup>b</sup>The years with alcohol dependence at gamete production age</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T2"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Result of variance component linkage analysis</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td></td><td></td><td align="center" colspan="2">Variance</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td colspan="2"><hr></hr></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="center">Chr</td><td align="center">Position (cM)</td><td align="center">Additive QTL</td><td align="center">Shared environmental factors</td><td align="center">LOD</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">259.84</td><td align="center">0.55</td><td align="center">0.37</td><td align="center">1.04</td></tr><tr><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">22.43</td><td align="center">0.65</td><td align="center">0.30</td><td align="center">1.09</td></tr><tr><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">40.55</td><td align="center">0.57</td><td align="center">0.36</td><td align="center">1.23</td></tr><tr><td align="center">6</